To identify cost-saving opportunities using Azure Advisor

Step 1: Access Azure Advisor
        Azure Advisor dashboard.
Step 2: Analyze Recommendations for Your Resources
        shut down underutilized virtual machines
        Optimize or remove idle public IP addresses, unattached disks, or unused resources.
        Switch to cheaper SKU or tier for services like App Service Plans or Databases
Step 3: Example Cost-Saving Proposal
        App Service Plans are underutilized, consider scaling to a lower pricing tier.
        Optimization: Switch from Premium to Standard or Basic tiers based on performance needs.
                      Delete disks no longer attached to VMs and disassociate unused public IPs.
                      Resize the VM to a smaller SKU or deallocate it if not in use.
Step 4: Implement and Monitor
         Monitor impact with Azure Cost Management + Billing dashboards.
         Use Azure Automation or Logic Apps for automated cleanup of idle resources.
         Set budget alerts to prevent unexpected costs.

